[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"commandExecution","id":"call_NurhHbEWzQFsg06fHJcheJ9f","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/resistor.md && sed -n '1,160p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/capacitor.md && sed -n '1,160p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/crystal.md\"","cwd":"/workspace","processId":"52499","source":"unifiedExecStartup","status":"completed","commandActions":[{"type":"read","command":"sed -n '1,180p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/resistor.md","name":"resistor.md","path":"/root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/resistor.md"},{"type":"read","command":"sed -n '1,160p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/capacitor.md","name":"capacitor.md","path":"/root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/capacitor.md"},{"type":"read","command":"sed -n '1,160p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/crystal.md","name":"crystal.md","path":"/root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/crystal.md"}],"aggregatedOutput":"# `<resistor />`\n\nA `<resistor />` is an extremely common element of electronic designs. It limits the flow of electricity and is critical to making sure digital signals are properly \"pulled up\" or \"pulled down\" to set their default value as `1` or `0`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nexport default () => (\n <board width=\"10mm\" height=\"10mm\">\n    <resistor\n      name=\"R1\"\n      footprint=\"0402\"\n      resistance=\"1k\"\n    />\n </board>\n)\n```\n\n## Props\n\nCommonly used: `resistance`, `tolerance`, `pullupFor`, `pullupTo`, `pulldownFor`, `pulldownTo`, `schOrientation`, `schSize`\n\n## References\n\n- Props: [ResistorProps](https://github.com/tscircuit/props#resistorprops-resistor)\n- Source: [lib/components/resistor.ts](https://github.com/tscircuit/props/blob/main/lib/components/resistor.ts)\n- Local docs: [docs/docs/elements/resistor.mdx](../docs/docs/elements/resistor.mdx)\n# `<capacitor />`\n\nA `<capacitor />` stores electrical energy in an electric field. Capacitors are commonly used for filtering, energy storage, and timing circuits. Unlike resistors, capacitors can be polarized (like electrolytic capacitors) or non-polarized (like ceramic capacitors).\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nexport default () => (\n <board width=\"10mm\" height=\"10mm\">\n  <capacitor\n    name=\"C2\"\n    footprint=\"axial_p5mm\"\n    capacitance=\"10μF\"\n    polarized\n  /> \n</board>\n)\n```\n\n## Props\n\nCommonly used: `capacitance`, `maxVoltageRating`, `schShowRatings`, `polarized`, `decouplingFor`, `decouplingTo`, `bypassFor`, `bypassTo`\n\n## References\n\n- Props: [CapacitorProps](https://github.com/tscircuit/props#capacitorprops-capacitor)\n- Source: [lib/components/capacitor.ts](https://github.com/tscircuit/props/blob/main/lib/components/capacitor.ts)\n- Local docs: [docs/docs/elements/capacitor.mdx](../docs/docs/elements/capacitor.mdx)\n# `<crystal />`\n\nA crystal oscillator provides a stable clock signal essential for timing applications and microcontroller operations.\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nexport default () => (\n  <board width=\"50mm\" height=\"50mm\">\n    <crystal\n      name=\"XT1\"\n      frequency=\"16MHz\"\n      loadCapacitance=\"18pF\"\n      footprint=\"hc49\"\n    />\n  </board>\n)\n```\n\n## Props\n\nCommonly used: `frequency`, `loadCapacitance`, `manufacturerPartNumber`, `mpn`, `pinVariant`, `schOrientation`, `connections`, `name`\n\n## References\n\n- Props: [CrystalProps](https://github.com/tscircuit/props#crystalprops-crystal)\n- Source: [lib/components/crystal.ts](https://github.com/tscircuit/props/blob/main/lib/components/crystal.ts)\n- Local docs: [docs/docs/elements/crystal.mdx](../docs/docs/elements/crystal.mdx)\n","exitCode":0,"durationMs":0},"threadId":"019e8ebd-60bc-75b1-a46a-4937607d5d0e","turnId":"019e8ebd-60c9-7312-b700-7779729e8d51","completedAtMs":1780511342449}}
