[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_007e7fd59c6c7e26016a2075d62f0481909f9098064053f7c7","text":"Implemented the RP2040 breakout in [index.circuit.tsx](/workspace/index.circuit.tsx).\n\nWhat’s included:\n- RP2040 local QFN-style footprint, no tscircuit registry imports\n- USB-C port, 5.1k CC pulldowns, USB D+/D- series resistors\n- 3.3 V LDO from USB VBUS\n- QSPI flash, 12 MHz crystal, decoupling caps\n- RUN and BOOT buttons\n- GPIO LED on GP25\n- 8-pin breakout/debug header: `VBUS`, `3V3`, `GND`, `RUN`, `SWCLK`, `SWD`, `GP0`, `GP1`\n- Top and bottom GND pours\n- No `routingDisabled` or `--routing-disabled` used\n\nValidation:\n- `npm run typecheck`: passed\n- `tsci check netlist index.circuit.tsx`: 0 errors, 0 warnings\n- `tsci check placement index.circuit.tsx`: 0 errors, 0 warnings\n- `tsci build index.circuit.tsx`: wrote `dist/index/circuit.json`, but tscircuit’s autorouter still reports one unsolved internal node `cmn_18`. Build exits code 0, but with routing errors.\n\n**TSCircuit Developer Feedback**\n- Confusing/surprising: `<trace>` produced a clean netlist, but build still reported many “missing trace” messages after autorouter failure.\n- Wasted most time: diagnosing autorouter failure around an opaque internal node name, `cmn_18`.\n- Helpful changes: tooling should map failed autorouter nodes back to source nets and component pins.\n- Specific friction: React `key` warnings appear for generated footprint pad arrays, but adding `key` directly causes TypeScript prop errors on tscircuit elements.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019e8ebd-60bc-75b1-a46a-4937607d5d0e","turnId":"019e8ebd-60c9-7312-b700-7779729e8d51","completedAtMs":1780512223177}}
